            .container { flex-direction: column; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="column">
            <h1>Why is the sky blue?</h1>
            <h2>For a 3-Year-Old</h2>
            <p>The sky is blue because the sunlight hits the air and scatters the blue color everywhere. The blue light likes to bounce around more than the other colors, so when you look up, you see blue all over the place!</p>
            <h2>For a High School Teenager</h2>
            <p>The sky appears blue due to a phenomenon called Rayleigh scattering. Sunlight is made of all the colors of the rainbow. When this light enters Earth's atmosphere, it crashes with gas molecules and particles. Blue light travels in shorter, smaller waves, so it gets scattered much more strongly than red light, filling our eyes with blue color from every direction in the sky.</p>
            <h2>For a Physics PhD</h2>
            <p>The azure hue of the sky is primarily the result of Rayleigh scattering of electromagnetic radiation by particles much smaller than the wavelength of the incident light (primarily nitrogen and oxygen molecules). The scattering intensity $I$ is proportional to the fourth power of the frequency ($\nu^{-4}$); since blue light occupies the higher end of the visible spectrum compared to red, it is scattered significantly more efficiently. While violet is scattered even more, the spectral radiance of the sun and the human eye's sensitivity to blue result in the perception of a blue-violet sky.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="column">
            <h1>为什么天空是蓝色的？</h1>
            <h2>给 3 岁宝宝</h2>
            <p>天空是蓝色的，因为阳光击中空气并将蓝光散射到各处。蓝光比其他颜色更喜欢到处蹦跳，所以当你抬头看时，你会看到到处都是蓝色的！</p>
            <h2>给高中生</h2>
            <p>天空看起来是蓝色的，是因为一种被称为瑞利散射（Rayleigh scattering）的现象。阳光由彩虹中的所有颜色组成。当这些光进入地球大气层时，它们会与气体分子和颗粒碰撞。蓝光的波长更短、更小，因此它比红光散射得强烈得多，从天空的各个方向用蓝色填充了我们的眼睛。</p>
            <h2>给物理学博士</h2>
            <p>天空的青蓝色调主要是由于远小于入射光波长的粒子（主要是氮气和氧分子）对电磁辐射的瑞利散射引起的。散射强度 $I$ 与频率的四次方 ($\nu^{-4}$) 成正比；由于与红光相比，蓝光占据可见光谱的高端，因此其散射效率显著更高。虽然紫光的散射更为剧烈，但太阳的光谱以及人眼对蓝色的敏感性导致了对蓝紫色天空的感知。</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
